

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FRA
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

class FRA(IRSwap):
    """Forward rate agreement — an :class:`IRSwap` that settles on its start date.

    Construction, schedule generation, forward projection and the reset /
    fixing interface are inherited unchanged, so a FRA is specified exactly
    like the equivalent single-period swap: ``effective_date`` is the start of
    the contract period (and the settlement date), ``maturity_date`` is the end
    of the period the rate accrues over.

    The single difference is settlement timing.  A FRA pays at the START of its
    contract period rather than in arrears at the end, so the trade is
    extinguished on ``effective_date`` and carries no exposure after it —
    ``scenario_npvs`` returns zero from the day after settlement onwards, in
    the same way :class:`IRSwap` returns zero past ``maturity_date``.

    Valuation up to and including the settlement date is unchanged.  The amount
    actually paid on ``effective_date`` is the period cashflow discounted back
    from the period end at the realized rate,

        N (L - K) tau / (1 + L tau)

    and since ``1 / (1 + L tau)`` is the discount factor over the period, its
    present value is what discounting ``N (L - K) tau`` from the period end
    already gives.  Settling early therefore moves *when* the exposure stops
    without changing the PV before then.

    Note that this equivalence is exact only when the forecast and discount
    curves coincide.  Under multi-curve discounting (e.g. a JIBAR-3M forecast
    leg discounted on ZAR-SWAP) market FRAs discount the settlement at the
    realized FRA rate itself while this class discounts on the discount curve,
    leaving a small basis between the two.  That matches how the equivalent
    swaplet is valued here, which is the intended behaviour.
    """

    def scenario_npvs(
        self,
        val_date: date,
        market_state: dict[str, RiskFactorSlice],
        fixings: dict[tuple[str, date], np.ndarray] | None = None,
        rng: np.random.Generator | None = None,
    ) -> np.ndarray:
        # Settled on the effective date — no exposure beyond it.  The
        # settlement date itself still values, mirroring IRSwap's treatment of
        # its own maturity date.
        if val_date > self.effective_date:
            disc_slice: CurveSlice = market_state[self.discount_curve_name]
            return np.zeros(disc_slice.values.shape[0])

        return super().scenario_npvs(val_date, market_state, fixings, rng)
